tensorChat

A powerful, flexible, and model-agnostic chat interface powered by Langchain. tensorChat enables seamless interaction with local and cloud-based LLMs, allowing users to inject context from files, websites, commands, and past chats—all managed through a unified context window architecture.

⸻

🚀 Features

🔌 Model Support & Prompt Handling
	•	Langchain-Powered Backend – Unified interface for all models (local or cloud).
	•	Multi-Model Support – Compatible with Ollama, Code LLaMA, Mistral, OpenAI, Claude, Anthropic, and more.
	•	Prompt Templates – Customizable prompts per model using PromptProcessorFactory.
	•	Streaming Tokens – Real-time streaming for supported models.

💬 Context & Chat Management
	•	Topic-Based Chats – Persistent chat threads with unique message IDs.
	•	Unified Context Window – Langchain handles all memory across models.
	•	Dynamic Context Injection:
	•	@add_context file.md – Load file content.
	•	@add_context topic:45 – Reuse past chat threads.
	•	@grab https://example.com – Use webpage content.
	•	@grab_output "df -h" – Use shell command output.
	•	@load path/to/file.txt – Inject file directly into prompt.

📋 Message Actions & Commands
	•	@copy 224 – Copy entire output of a message.
	•	@copycode 225 – Copy code blocks only.
	•	@run 226 – Execute message output as shell command.
	•	Save any command output to file or context (@grab_output "uptime" > sys.txt).

🧠 AI Utilities
	•	@summary – Summarize the current thread.
	•	@summarize topic:xyz – Summarize any past topic.
	•	Merge multiple context types into a single input.

☁️ Cloud Settings Sync
	•	Backup/load your config and sessions to/from:
	•	Dropbox
	•	Amazon S3
	•	Google Drive
	•	Auto-sync and cross-device setup supported.

⚙️ Extensibility & Configuration
	•	Settings File – ~/.config/chatui/settings.ini
	•	Factory Architecture – Easily extend core components (PromptProcessor, ChatState, etc).
	•	Plugin-Ready – Add custom commands, formatters, and model wrappers.

